---
// "Build once. Quote anywhere.": the three-step flow + code sample.
const py = `from costql import PricingPack

pack = PricingPack.load("tmdb_t3.json")          # one static file
quote = pack.quote('{ movie(id:"27205"){ cast(limit:8){ person{ name } } } }')

quote["price"]         # 50.5   safe max: price on this to never undercharge
quote["typical_price"] # 36.4   typical: what the query usually costs
quote["confidence"]    # "high"`;

const js = `import { PricingPack } from "costql";

const pack = await PricingPack.load("tmdb_t3.json");  // the same file
const quote = pack.quote('{ movie(id:"27205"){ cast(limit:8){ person{ name } } } }');

quote.price          // 50.5   safe max: price on this to never undercharge
quote.typical_price  // 36.4   typical: what the query usually costs
quote.confidence     // "high"`;
---

<section id="build" class="cql-build">
  <div class="cql-container cql-section">
  <h2 class="cql-h2">Build once. Quote anywhere.</h2>
  <p class="cql-lead">
    Three steps take you from a live endpoint to a pricing pack your app carries with it.
  </p>

  <div class="cql-steps__flow">
    <div class="cql-card cql-step">
      <div class="cql-step__head">
        <span class="cql-step__num">step 1</span>
        <h3>Adapt</h3>
      </div>
      <p>
        Tell costQL where your API lives and give it a few real IDs to query with. That's
        a short adapter file, about 90 lines. Three finished examples ship in the repo.
      </p>
      <a href="/docs/adapters/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The adapter guide →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="cql-steps__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>

    <div class="cql-card cql-step">
      <div class="cql-step__head">
        <span class="cql-step__num">step 2</span>
        <h3>Build</h3>
      </div>
      <p>
        Run <code>costql build</code>. It sends calibration queries to your API, times the
        answers, and saves everything it learned as one JSON file: the pricing pack.
      </p>
      <span class="cql-badge">schema + rates + fees → one JSON</span>
    </div>

    <div class="cql-steps__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>

    <div class="cql-card cql-step">
      <div class="cql-step__head">
        <span class="cql-step__num">step 3</span>
        <h3>Quote</h3>
      </div>
      <p>
        Load the pack in Python or JavaScript and price queries right where your code runs,
        with no more calls to your API. Both languages give the exact same answer.
      </p>
      <a href="/docs/quickstart/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Quote your first pack →</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cql-callout cql-callout--panel">
    <span class="cql-callout__label">Outside calls, too:</span>
    <span>
      some fields call an outside service for you: an LLM, a licensed data feed. costQL can't
      know what that service charges, so it names the call and your app puts the price on it. <a
      href="/docs/external-calls/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">External calls</a> shows how.
    </span>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 24px">
    <div class="cql-code" id="quote-sample">
      <div class="cql-code__head">
        <button class="cql-code__tab cql-code__tab--active" data-lang="py">python</button>
        <button class="cql-code__tab" data-lang="js">node.js</button>
        <button class="cql-code__copy" data-copy-code aria-label="copy code" title="copy to clipboard">
          <svg class="cql-code__ic-copy" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <rect x="9" y="9" width="12" height="12" rx="1.5" />
            <path d="M5 15H4a1.5 1.5 0 0 1-1.5-1.5v-9A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 4 3h9A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 14.5 4.5V5" />
          </svg>
          <svg class="cql-code__ic-check" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5" />
          </svg>
        </button>
      </div>
      <pre data-lang="py">{py}</pre>
      <pre data-lang="js" hidden>{js}</pre>
    </div>
  </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script is:inline>
  {
    const box = document.getElementById('quote-sample');
    box.querySelectorAll('.cql-code__tab').forEach((tab) => {
      tab.addEventListener('click', () => {
        box.querySelectorAll('.cql-code__tab').forEach((t) =>
          t.classList.toggle('cql-code__tab--active', t === tab));
        box.querySelectorAll('pre').forEach((pre) => {
          pre.hidden = pre.dataset.lang !== tab.dataset.lang;
        });
      });
    });

    const copy = box.querySelector('[data-copy-code]');
    copy.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const shown = box.querySelector('pre:not([hidden])');
      try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(shown?.textContent || ''); } catch {}
      copy.classList.add('cql-code__copy--copied');
      setTimeout(() => copy.classList.remove('cql-code__copy--copied'), 1200);
    });
  }
</script>
